# School as Studio: Learning through the Arts.

**Authors:** Stevens, Karen

## Abstract
Asserts that arts can be catalysts for learning and should be a basic part of students' education, describing the traditional school as factory model of education versus school as studio, which uses the arts as a vehicle for curriculum. The paper examines the status of arts education, discusses alternative paths to reform that acknowledge arts as equally as important as science and humanities, and describes creative applications of the arts. (SM)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ662087

